==================================================================================
S716 — the A+B+C-D-E-F+G recurrence: relations & computational tricks
==================================================================================

(1) A+B+C-D-E-F+G = inclusion-exclusion over B_3; d-simplex => (x-1)^(d+1)
   pieces = 2^3-1=7 subsets; signs (+,+,+,-,-,-,+) = (-1)^(|S|+1) = Mobius of B_3.
   d=1 (1-simplex): corner-IE sum_{k}(-1)^(k+1)C(2,k)N(n-k)=N(n)? True; Delta^2 N == 0? True  (N(n)=C(n+0,1), degree 1)
   d=2 (2-simplex): corner-IE sum_{k}(-1)^(k+1)C(3,k)N(n-k)=N(n)? True; Delta^3 N == 0? True  (N(n)=C(n+1,2), degree 2)
   d=3 (3-simplex): corner-IE sum_{k}(-1)^(k+1)C(4,k)N(n-k)=N(n)? True; Delta^4 N == 0? True  (N(n)=C(n+2,3), degree 3)
   d=4 (4-simplex): corner-IE sum_{k}(-1)^(k+1)C(5,k)N(n-k)=N(n)? True; Delta^5 N == 0? True  (N(n)=C(n+3,4), degree 4)
   => the user's triangle is the d=2 case: 3 corners, char poly (x-1)^3, quadratic cells.

(2) RELATION+TRICK A (additive/valuative): exact IE => Delta^3=0 => quadratic; 3 seeds suffice
   #tiles C(n-1,2): minimal recurrence order 3, coeffs ['3', '-3', '1']  (expect 3; 3,-3,1)
   3-seed reconstruction of #tiles from [1,3,6]: [1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21, 28, 36]  (= [1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21, 28, 36])
   EXACT valuative IE on arcs: A+B+C-D-E-F+G = 28, full arc-count = 28  (match: True)  <- additive invariants obey the IE exactly

(3) RELATION+TRICK B (multiplicative): H of a recursive family is C-finite => O(log n) matrix power
   base-path H (direct DP, k=1..9): [1, 5, 17, 57, 193, 653, 2209, 7473, 25281]
   AUTO-DISCOVERED recurrence: order 3, coeffs ['3', '1', '1']  (THM-337: 3,1,1)
   matrix-power H at k=20,50,100 (O(log k), DP infeasible): [56804250945, 429880204100371119351881425, 125398342137678662920398883435677708138480256488441793]
   cross-check k=9: matrix-power=25281 vs DP=25281  (match: True)

(4) THE BOUNDARY: A038375 (max-H over ALL tournaments) is NOT C-finite (no low-order recurrence)
   A038375 minimal recurrence (order<=5): NONE FOUND  => the trick needs a fixed FAMILY (bounded boundary width), not the optimum.
